Cell["\<\
The Ohm (\[CapitalOmega]) is the unit of resistance. The symbol R and circuit \
symbol shown above are often used in reference to resistors.The image shows a \
10 k\[CapitalOmega] metal film resistor. 
Metal film resistors behave as ideal resistors up to moderately high \
frequencies (e.g., 1 MHz). Metal film resistors like the one shown above are \
commonly available in the range 1 \[CapitalOmega] to 10 M\[CapitalOmega]. \
Specialized resistors are available outside this range (e.g., 0.1 \
\[CapitalOmega] power resistors). There are a few other types of resistors \
(e.g., wire wound, carbon film). Carbon film resistors sometimes change value \
in the process of soldering them in place.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.792759648282717*^9, 3.792759687373875*^9}, {
  3.7927598189006844`*^9, 3.7927598422037945`*^9}, {3.792759900028031*^9, 
  3.7927599634331803`*^9}, {3.7927600643860536`*^9, 3.792760129227604*^9}, {
  3.792760218997295*^9, 3.792760263324597*^9}, {3.792760394191565*^9, 
  3.7927605119882917`*^9}, {3.792769133915352*^9, 3.792769290170932*^9}, {
  3.792769771081478*^9, 3.792769776507006*^9}, {3.792769953068821*^9, 
  3.7927699574765806`*^9}, {3.792770003927413*^9, 
  3.792770005755448*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ed3f08e2-9033-45ca-842b-\
54191c7cfbd4"],

Cell["The electrical impedance of an ideal resistor is:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.792760621922182*^9, 3.792760633028642*^9}, {
  3.792767539773631*^9, 
  3.792767558842907*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"61fb4b70-e10c-4a24-aaee-\
abc945cb3773"],

