Cell["\<\
Notice that at low frequencies (10 Hz to 1 kHz) the LCR circuit behaves as a \
capacitor (gain slope of -1 and phase of -90 deg) and at higher frequencies \
(10 kHz to 1 MHz) the LCR circuit behaves like an inductor (gain slope of +1 \
and phase of +90 deg).

If we can lower the series resistance even further we can get a sharper dip \
in the impedance gain:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.792766733796895*^9, 3.792766812161793*^9}, {
  3.792767335113457*^9, 3.792767392072953*^9}, {3.7927674269593925`*^9, 
  3.792767431118195*^9}, {3.7927687559626875`*^9, 3.792768756416023*^9}, {
  3.792770210807773*^9, 3.792770257881145*^9}, {3.7927717086998177`*^9, 
  3.7927719688635845`*^9}, {3.950866516557019*^9, 3.9508665731193457`*^9}, {
  3.95086667306798*^9, 3.950866697791748*^9}, {3.9512401774873343`*^9, 
  3.951240231341317*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"238c9572-97a6-4f8b-bd17-\
a46df62d5635"],

